  "notes": "Confidence metrics describe aspects of a predicted structure. ipSAE derives interface confidence from predicted aligned errors rather than measuring binding free energy. Binding and kinetic measurements establish interaction under stated conditions. Functional readouts address the intended biological effect. Further development needs exposure, stability and safety evidence, followed by clinical evaluation. Evidence usually grows iteratively. Each row separates the claim directly supported by a readout from the next question.\n\nSources\n[AF3] Abramson et al. Accurate structure prediction of biomolecular interactions with AlphaFold 3. Nature (2024)\nhttps://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-024-07487-w\n\n[IPSAE] Dunbrack. Res ipSAE loquunt: What's wrong with AlphaFold's ipTM score and how to fix it. bioRxiv (2025)\nhttps://doi.org/10.1101/2025.02.10.637595\nhttps://github.com/DunbrackLab/IPSAE\n\n[FDA] US FDA. Discovery and Development\nhttps://www.fda.gov/patients/drug-development-process/step-1-discovery-and-development\n\n[FDA-PROCESS] US FDA. The Drug Development Process\nhttps://www.fda.gov/patients/learn-about-drug-and-device-approvals/drug-development-process\n\nSource check: 8 November 2026. Representative tools, not an exhaustive ranking."
